  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.8.11: JxlLayers reads the layers of a layered still image as separate images (as djxl --no_coalescing does), each with its offset, name, blend mode and clamp, plus Flatten(), which is exactly the Image.Load result. Load, LoadAsync and Identify for files, streams and memory; the image is decoded once through Image.Load with the same options and limits, every layer counted against MaxPixels and MaxFrames; ApplyExifOrientation orients layers and offsets like libjxl. Image.Load results are unchanged. See docs/releases/release-0.8.11.md and docs/design/0.8.11-layers.md.",
